      "id": "r3",
      "type": "stanza_note",
      "lines": [
        {
          "n": 1,
          "text": "सत्यमेव व्रतं तदेव व्यसनं येषां ते as given in the commentary and in",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 2,
          "text": "Râmarshi is inaccurate. It should be तस्मिन्व्यसनिनः Râmarshi reads",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 3,
          "text": "लज्जाम् and explains it by अकार्यकरणात् ह्रियम् and he also reads",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 4,
          "text": "",
          "end": "join"
        },
        {
          "n": 5,
          "text": "अनुवर्तमानाः to which लज्जाम् is taken as the object.—Vasantatilakâ.",
          "end": "space"
        }
      ],
      "uncertain": false,
      "note": null
    },
    {
      "id": "r4",
      "type": "heading",
      "lines": [
        {
          "n": 1,
          "text": "",
          "end": "join"
        },
        {
          "n": 2,
          "text": "MISCELLANEOUS.",
          "end": "space"
        }
      ],
      "uncertain": false,
      "note": null
    },
    {
      "id": "r5",
      "type": "stanza_note",
      "lines": [
        {
          "n": 1,
          "text": "Stanza I.—भावः. For the meaning of this word see Raghu II.,",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 2,
          "text": "26 and Kumâra. III., 68 with Mallinâtha’s comments on those two",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 3,
          "text": "",
          "end": "join"
        },
        {
          "n": 4,
          "text": "passages. See also Sṛingâras'ataka 2, where the commentator ren-",
          "end": "hyphen"
        },
        {
          "n": 5,
          "text": "ders it by चित्ताभिप्राय as Râmarshi renders it here. सूक्ष्ममार्ग = अलभ्यमार्ग",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 6,
          "text": "(commentary in M.) a narrow path. पुष्करपत्त्रतोय is a very common",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 7,
          "text": "simile for every thing fickle, unsteady. आशंसितः in the sense of शंसित",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 8,
          "text": "not the more usual hoped or expected. The defects pointed out",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 9,
          "text": "in the first three lines like germs of poison develop as a woman",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 10,
          "text": "grows. नाम is an idiomatic expletive equivalent to “verily” com-",
          "end": "hyphen"
        },
        {
          "n": 11,
          "text": "pare note to St. 20. The commentary in M. and Râmarshi have",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 12,
          "text": "नामेति संबोधने which is not quite intelligible; should it be संभावने ?",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 13,
          "text": "See note Stanza 57 supra.—S'ârdûlavikrîḍita.",
          "end": "space"
        }
      ],
      "uncertain": false,
      "note": null
    },
    {
      "id": "r6",
      "type": "stanza_note",
      "lines": [
        {
          "n": 1,
          "text": "St. II.—अभिमुख i. e. in battle. For the idea of the first line",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 2,
          "text": "comp. Bhagavadgîtâ II., 38 Manu VII., 89 or the following",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 3,
          "text": "Stanza quoted by Madhusûdana Sarasvatî under Gîtâ I., 31 द्वाविमौ",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 4,
          "text": "पुरुषौ लोके सूर्यमण्डलभेदिनौ । परिव्राड्योगयुक्तश्च रणे चाभिमुखो हतः ॥ “Praise",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 5,
          "text": "",
          "end": "join"
        },
        {
          "n": 6,
          "text": "",
          "end": "join"
        },
        {
          "n": 7,
          "text": "from both armies is exceedingly pleasant to the ear.” The Stanza",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 8,
          "text": "means that whether a man killed in the front ranks in a battle",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 9,
          "text": "does or does not obtain victory or heaven, he certainly must ob-",
          "end": "hyphen"
        },
        {
          "n": 10,
          "text": "tain the eulogy of both sides, and that is very substantial gain.",
          "end": "space"
        },
        {
          "n": 11,
          "text": "The reading of M. as will be seen is different. But I do not",
          "end": "space"
        }
      ],
      "uncertain": false,
      "note": null
    },
